    {
      "id": "D1",
      "at": "2026-08-09T10:05:00Z",
      "scope": "change",
      "made_by": "leader",
      "decision": "Branched CH4 off ft/RM7-history-graph-improvements (7d0445b) rather than main.",
      "why": "This change rewrites buildBatteryChart, the same function RM7 tier 2 just modified, and depends on Snapshot.EffectiveDate from RM7 tier 1. Branching off main would conflict on both. Consequence: CH4 cannot merge before RM7 does.",
      "covered_by": null
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "at": "2026-08-09T10:05:00Z",
      "scope": "change",
      "made_by": "user",
      "decision": "The negative-delta (charging day) question is deliberately LEFT OPEN in the proposal, not resolved.",
      "why": "User explicitly asked to record it for later: their preferred direction is adding back the level charged that day from Supercharger + manual charge records. Artifacts ship clamp-to-zero as provisional behaviour with the three options documented for a follow-up grill-me.",
      "covered_by": "design.md Open Questions"
    }
  ],
  "events": [
    {
      "at": "2026-08-09T10:05:00Z",
      "agent": "leader",
      "event": "Artifacts created by the gateway worker and validated (openspec validate --strict passed). Leader independently verified the worker's data-source findings: telemetry.SuperchargerReader.SuperchargerSessionsByVehicle (EnergyKWh), manualcharge.Entry.EnergyAddedKWh, and battery.RecentEfficiency all exist as claimed - so open-question option 3 is more feasible than the dispatch assumed. No DB object proposed, so no design gate. HALTED AFTER ARTIFACTS per the user's request for a proposal only."
